course: dictionary
lesson: 2254
title: Strong wishes: craving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A craving is a very strong wish for something, especially a food or a drink. Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «Pregnant mothers are said to have unusual cravings.» Here the clue is the word unusual: a craving is a strong wish, and some are strange.
explain: Craving can also be a verb. The verb is crave, and it changes its form: crave, craves, craved, craving. «The Buddha taught that suffering comes from craving, always wanting more.» Here craving is the -ing form of crave, so it means wanting something very strongly.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Toad feels the old craving creep over him again.» If you swap in a strong wish, the sentence still makes sense. That is a good sign your meaning is right.
fact: A craving is a very strong wish for something, often a food or a drink.
fact: «Craving» can be a noun (a craving, cravings) or the -ing form of the verb «crave».
fact: Phrases to know: «a craving for», «satisfy a craving», «crave attention».
fact: In Buddhism, craving (always wanting more) is taught as a cause of suffering.
exercise: «She had a craving for cold lemonade after school.» What does craving mean here? | A loud shout of surprise | *A very strong wish for something | A cold drink of water | A chore she must do
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of the verb «crave»? | *craving | crate | crazy | cravat
exercise: «The Buddha taught that suffering comes from craving, always wanting more.» What does the sentence suggest craving is? | Sleeping well at night | A kind of soup | *Always wanting more | Being happy with what you have
test: Pregnant mothers are said to have «unusual cravings». What are cravings here? | Sudden naps | *Strong wishes for certain foods | Tiny insects that fly | Lessons at school
test: Toad asks to sit in the front seat «for the fresh air», as «the old craving creeps over him again». What does the craving make him want? | To sleep in the garden | To hide from the driver | To go to school | *To sit in the front seat again
exam: In which sentence is craving a noun? | She craves cold lemonade every day. | He craved the cake yesterday. | *She had a craving for cold lemonade. | They are craving a rest.
